  "body": "PR #1156 (#547) ships the MCP tool `electrode_from_faces` (`crates/app/src/mcp/sinker_tools.rs`) over the undoable `ElectrodeFromFaces` command. The camcraft-mcp skill (`.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md`) is a process file, so the feature PR leaves its tool table alone and this row is owed (asked for in NeoTech's review of #1156 at dcaa3a36).\n\nDone means: once #1156 has merged, the camcraft-mcp skill's tool table has an `electrode_from_faces` row. It names the arguments (`name`, `picks`, `undersize` or `condition` (exactly one), `setup` (only with `condition`), `orbit`, `stub`, `pickup`) and the reply (`electrode`, `cavity`, a `burn` object that `add_operation` takes as is, `frame: world`, `note`, `warning`). The PR bumps `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION`, as process changes do.\n\nPart of #547.\n",
